<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 31,000 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 46.690 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 19,500 tonnes, in Belgium 5,000, in Germany 3,000, in the U.K. 3,000 and in Finland 500 tonnes, it added.  </p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, London traders had expected the subsidy for the current season whites campaign to be 46.690 Ecus per 100 kilos, the exact amount awarded.</p>
<p>Traders had also forecast the total authorised sugar tonnage export awards to be less than 60,000 tonnes versus 88,250 last week when the restitution was 46.704 Ecus.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
